  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="6.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ICn">I Cn</ref> 6.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="6.2" corresp="#wit-g-a">Fullgeorne hig witan, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> hig nagon mid rihte þurh hæmedþingc wifes gemanan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="6.2" corresp="#wit-a">Fullgeorne hi witan, þæt hig nagon mid rihte þurh hæmedþinge wifes gemanan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="6.2" corresp="#wit-d-frags">Fulgeorne we witan, þæt hi nagan mid rihte þurh hæmedþingc wifes gemánan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="6.2" corresp="#wit-q">quia perfecte sciunt: non est rectum, ut causa cohabitandi cum mulieribus habitent.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="6a.2" corresp="#wit-g-a">Fullgeorne hig witan þæt hig nagon mid rihte þurh hæmedþingc wifes gemanan.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-g-a">They know full well that they have no right to marry.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Recht genau wissen sie (wir D), dass sie von Rechts wegen keine Gemeinschaft mit einer Frau durch Beischlaf haben dürfen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">They (we, D) know full well that they may not lawfully have intercourse with a woman.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares V Atr 9.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
